T-NEWC-P1 [1219fe78c446] BLUF: the chat routes keep the words of one kind of error and send the client a constant for every other, and the rule that picks that kind is the error's code string AI_ENDPOINT_REDIRECT_REFUSED (chatErrorText, backend/server.js line 1437; the same string is tested on the chat routes at lines 7598 and 7653). The independent review of pull request 229 (first round) measured with node and no server that the AI client library copies the code of an error from the endpoint's HTTP error body: its APIError built from a 400 or a 500 body that carries that code has that code, chatErrorText then returns the status and the endpoint's own text, and the control code Other gives the constant. So an AI endpoint that answers with that code can put its own text into a stream error event, and the chat page writes that event's message into the bubble with innerHTML and no escaping (static/js/index.js line 3512). The residual needs an administrator-configured endpoint that answers with exactly that code. Pre-existing and narrowed by pull request 229: before it, every thrown text reached those sinks (measured at base by the review: a GET stream with the model host answering 500 with a marker text sent the marker); after it, only a text carried under this one code does. It landed on main as merge commit 46050e25 (its first 8 characters) on 2026-11-19 11:04 AEDT.
T-NEWC-P2 [e37caf9bf247] Where (read at that merge commit, not run): the stream error events are written at server.js lines 7865, 7872, 7991 and 7998 through chatErrorText, and POST /api/chat puts the error's message into its error field at line 7653 for the same code. The page's stream reader handles an error event at static/js/index.js line 3512 by assigning a span that holds the event's message to innerHTML with no escape, while the same file writes model text through formatAIResponse (line 3466), which escapes HTML first (line 3577), and the answer of POST /api/chat reaches the page through addAIMessage, which calls formatAIResponse (line 3169), so that route is escaped. The adapter sets the code only in AiEndpointRedirectError (backend/llm/azureOpenAIAdapter.js line 110), with a constant message and a comment that it holds no angle brackets because the chat writes error messages through innerHTML (lines 103 and 104). The existing test file for the redirect refusal reads the stream's error events in cells C1 (line 546) and E4 (line 650) with a substring check on the real refusal's words; 0 lines of that file name an endpoint error body, a forged code or a spoof (control: the file's own name constant NAMED is on 12 lines). No open code scanning alert on main names static/js/index.js (22 open at the merge commit, read by path). Not measured by this note: the library's behaviour (relayed from the review), a browser render, and what the page's content security policy does with the text.
