**C-<<Cn1>>. DID NEXUSAI PULL REQUESTS 228 AND 229 LAND ON MAIN, WHAT DO THEY DO TO RD-1005 AND RD-1007, WHY DID THE HOSTED CODE SCAN CHECK STOP THE FIRST VERSION OF 229 AND WHAT DID THE SECOND VERSION CHANGE, AND WHAT STAYS OPEN? (landings recorded by the coordinator; it decides nothing new)** This entry is a record: it carries no ruling of its own and changes none; it touches the CodeQL policy (C-190) and the demo deploy hold (C-224) by reference only; any demo deploy is separate from this record. Provenance: pulls/228 and pulls/229 with their file lists and commits, the merge commits named below, the check-runs and workflow runs of each, the hosted code scan check runs and the two pull request analyses of the first and the second version, main's code scanning analyses and alerts read <<READ-DATE>> (<<CHECKS-LIST>>; <<BUILD-LIST>>; <<ALERTS>>), the two independent reviews of the branch of 229 (the gate's verdict of each round, read whole, kept outside this repository), the builders' records, the tickets and their comments, and the Jira reads and writes of <<READ-DATE>>. Nothing was built, run, sent or put on a host by this step.
